$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Substituted 3-Amino-4-(2-iodophenoxy)phenyl sulfones 11. A suspension of
substituted 2-iodophenol (20 mmol), 4-fluoro-3-nitrophenyl sulfone (10
mmol), and potassium carbonate (40 mmol) in dimethylsulfoxide (30 mL) was
heated at 55 °C for 8 h. After cooling to room temperature, the reaction
mixture was diluted with water (50 mL) and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 150 mL). The combined organic phase was washed with water (3 × 100
mL) and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The solvent was removed
under reduced pressure to give crude nitro halide used in the next step
without further purification. The solution of crude nitro halide and
tin(ΙΙ) chloride dihydrate (100 mmol) in ethyl acetate (100 mL) was
stirred at room temperature for 18 h. The reaction mixture was quenched
with aqueous sodium hydroxide, and the aqueous phase was extracted with
ethyl acetate (3 × 100 mL). The combined organic phase was washed with
water (3 × 100 mL) and dried over anhydrous magnesium sulfate. The
solvent was evaporated in vacuo, and the residue was purified by flash
chromatography on silica gel with a mixture of hexane and ethyl acetate
as eluant to afford the corresponding product.
3-Amino-4-(4-chloro-2-iodophenoxy)phenyl sulfone (11c). 76% yield; mp
204−205 °C; 1H NMR (300MHz, CD3SOCD3) δ 7.98 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 2H), 7.45
(dd, J = 2.3, 8.7 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (d, J = 2.3 Hz, 2H), 6.96 (dd, J = 2.1,
8.3 Hz, 4H), 6.62 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 2H), 5.64 (s, 4H); 13C NMR (300MHz,
CD3SOCD3) δ 155.06, 146.87, 140.93, 139.24, 137.71, 130.88, 129.95,
121.81, 117.72, 115.82, 113.88, 91.90; MS (EI) m/z 752 [M+]; HRMS Calcd.
for C24H16Cl2I2N2O4S 751.8297, found 751.8269.
