$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for preparing 2-nitrodiphenyl ethers 3a-k, 3n-o, and
3r-t The 2-nitrodiphenyl ethers were prepared via a modification of the
published synthetic procedure.1 Ethers 3a,2 3b,3 3f,3 3h4, 3n,5 3o,6
3r-s,7 and 3t8 are known compounds. To a mixture of potassium carbonate
and the substituted phenol in DMF, 1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene was added
dropwise while stirring under nitrogen. After 3 h at 80°C, 50 mL of water
and then 30 mL of ethyl acetate were added to the reaction mixture. The
organic layer was washed with water (50 mL x 3), and the products were
obtained by removal of the EtOAc. 1-Nitro-2-(p-tolyloxy)benzene (3a): 2
p-Cresol (0.21 g, 1.9 mmol), 1-fluoro-2-nitrobenzene (205 μL, 1.9 mmol),
and K2CO3 (1.3 g, 9.7 mmol) were used. The product was obtained as a
yellow solid (0.33 g, 75%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.93 (dd, J1 = 8.3
Hz, J2 = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.49-7.43 (m, 1H), 7.19-7.12 (m, 3H), 6.99-6.96 (m,
3H), 2.35 (s, 3H).
