$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Experimental Procedure for Tandem C-O, C-N Bond Formations (Scheme 2). To
an oven-dried screwed vial were added 4-bromochlorobenzene (76 mg, 0.4
mmol), 4-methoxyphenol (74 mg, 0.6 mmol), cesium carbonate (260 mg, 0.8
mmol), Rh(cod)(iPr-bimy)br (9 mg, 5 mol %), AgSbF6 (14 mg, 10 mol %),
Et3N (0.4 mL) and toluene (0.4 mL). The mixture was vigorously stirred at
100 °C for 24 h and diluted with diethyl ether. The crude reaction
mixture was filtered through a pad of silica gel and organic solvents
were removed in vacuo, and then it was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (EtOAc/n-Hx, 1:10). After this purification procedure,
product 3e was obtained. white solid (70 mg, 75%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 5 mol% Rh-NHC catalyst; 10 mol% silver salt
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Rhodium(NHC)-Catalyzed O-Arylation of Aryl Bromides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
