$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Synthesis of Diketones 8a-e and Triketone 8i.
Preparation of 8a. To a stirred mixture of p-hydroxyacetophenone 7a (15
g, 110 mmol) in dimethyl sulfoxide (50 mL) were added
p-fluoroacetophenone (15.22 g, 110 mmol, 1 equiv) and anhydrous K2CO3
(22.5 g, 160 mmol, 1.5 equiv), and the reaction mixture was refluxed for
2h with continuous stirring. The reaction mixture was cooled to room
temperature, diluted with water (100 mL), and extracted with ether (3 ×
200 mL). The organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and
concentrated to furnish a crude product, which on crystallization in a
mixture of benzene and hexane (3:7) furnished diketone 8a (21 g, 75%
yield) as a white solid, mp 98-100°C. Compounds 8b-e were prepared by the
above procedure by condensing p-fluoroacetophenone with
m-hydroxyacetophenone 7b, quinol 7c, 2,7-dihydroxynaphthalene 7d, and
1,5-dihydroxynaph-thalene 7e, respectively. Compound 8i was prepared by
condensing p-fluoroacetophenone with phluroglucinol 7i.
1-[4-(4-Acetylphenoxy)phenyl]ethanone (8a). Yield 75%, white solid, mp
98-100°C; IR (KBr, cm-1) 1678; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 2.57 (s, 6H),
7.06 (d, 4H, Ar, J= 8.8 Hz), 7.97 (d, 4H, Ar, J= 8.8 Hz); FAB-MS (m/z)
255 [M+H]+.
