$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Copper-Catalyzed
O-Arylation of Aryl Iodides in the Presence of KF/Al2O3 (Table 1) To a
solution of aryl iodide (1 mmol) and phenol (3 mmol) in toluene (5 ml)
under an argon atmosphere, CuI (15 mol%) and 1,3-diphenyl-1,3
propanedione (15mol%) followed by KF/Al2O3[17] (5 equiv.) were added, and
the reaction was stirred at 100-110°C for the specified time (Table 1).
The progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC. The reaction mixture
was allowed to cool to room temperature, diluted with ethylacetate (30
ml), and filtered off. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced
pressure. The desired product was isolated by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane as eluent to afford the pure product. The
spectroscopic data and melting points for the known products agreed well
with the reported data. 2-(4-Methylphenoxy)-biphenyl ether (entry 16,
Table 1). White solid, yield 75% Mp: 48-49 °C, 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) = 7.61 (br d, J= 7.7Hz, 2H), 7.49 (dd, J= 7.5, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.40
(t, J= 7.5 Hz, 2H), 7.35-7.30 (m, 2H), 7.24- 7.22 (m, 1H), 7.11 (d, J=
8.4Hz, 2H), 7.02 (brd,J= 8.1 Hz, 1H), 6.88 (d, J= 6.5Hz, 2H), 2.34 (s,
3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Diaryl Ethers Through the Copper-Catalyzed Arylation of
Phenols with Aryl Iodides Using KF/Al2O3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hosseinzadeh, Rahman; Tajbakhsh, Mahmood; Mohadjerani, Maryam; Rezaei,
Parizad; Alikarami, Mohammad
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
