$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure B: synthesis of diarylether
precursors - 4.0 mmol scale (COR = ketone or ester) Typically, unless
otherwise noted, picolinic acid (99.0 mg, 0.8 mmol), CuI (76.2 mg, 0.4
mmol), and K3PO4 (1.272 g, 6.0 mmol) were weighed into an oven-dried
50-mL Schlenk tube. The tube was then evacuated and back-filled with
argon (this sequence was repeated a total 3 times), and dry DMSO (10 mL)
was added under argon via syringe. The tube was then placed in a
preheated oil bath at 50°C, and mixture was stirred for 10 minutes. In a
separate oven-dried tube, aryl chloride (4.0 mmol) and appropriate phenol
(6.0 mmol ) were weighed and the tube was evacuated and back-filled with
argon (this sequence was repeated a total 3 times). Dry DMSO (10 mL) was
then added under argon. The mixture was stirred at room temperature for
10 min and transferred into the catalyst Schlenk tube via syringe.
Reaction mixture was then placed in a preheated oil bath at 110 °C and
allowed to stir for 24 h. At the end of this time the tube was removed
from the bath, allowed to cool to room temperature, and the contents
diluted with EtOAc (20 mL). The mixture was filtered through a plug of
silica and poured into a separatory funnel, then washed with saturated
solution of NaHCO3 (20 mL), water (20 mL x 5) and diluted with ethyl
acetate (40 mL). Organic layer was separated and dried on Na2SO4, then
filtered. After concentration under reduced pressure, the crude mixture
was purified, either by silica gel chromatography, or by Biotage SP4
technique, eluting with hexanes/ethyl acetate/diethyl ether mixtures to
afford pure precursor (typically as colorless or light yellow oil).
(2-(2-bromophenoxy)phenyl)(phenyl)methanone (P14) Following general
procedure B: 2-hydroxybenzophenone (1.19 g, 6.0 mmol) and
1,2-dibromobenzene (936 mg, 4.0 mmol) were used. Chromatography: Biotage
SP4 (97% hexanes and 3% ethyl acetate) provided a pure precursor as
colorless oil. (2-(2-chloro-5-methoxyphenoxy)phenyl)(phenyl)methanone
(P17) Following general procedure B: 2-hydroxybenzophenone (1.188 g, 6.0
mmol) and 3-bromo-4-chloroanisole (1.096 g, 4.0 mmol) were used.
Chromatography: Biotage SP4 (95% hexanes and 5% ethyl acetate) provided a
pure adduct as a colorless oil. (1.13 mg - 75%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ: 7.86-7.84 (m, 2H), 7.55-7.48 (m, 2H), 7.43-7.39 (m, 3H), 7.20-7.16 (m,
2H), 6.80-6.78 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 6.58-6.55 (dd, J 1 = 8.8 Hz, J 2 =
2.8 Hz, 1H), 6.47-6.46 (d, J = 2.8 Hz, 1H), 3.67 (s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 195.57, 159.31, 154.20, 152.16, 137.47, 133.18,
131.97, 130.68, 130.42, 130.20, 129.99, 128.27, 123.33, 117.29, 117.26,
110.90, 106.98, 55.65 ppm. IR (KBr disc, cm-1): 1669, 1599, 1572, 1482,
1443, 1317, 1293, 1217, 1161, 1070, 1027, 927, 758, 702, 635.
