$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Synthetic Procedure of Functionalized Bis-p-Nitrophenoxy
Derivatives In a three-necked round flask equipped with condenser,
magnetic stirring bar, nitrogen inlet and a dropping funnel, were placed
anhydrous K2CO3 (6.9 g, 50 mmol), a functionalized phenol (1, 3-5, 10
meq) and freshly distilled anhydrous CH3CN (100 mL). The reaction mixture
was heated to refluxing temperature; to this stirred suspension a
solution of 1-fluoro-4-nitrobenzene (11 meq) in freshly distilled CH3CN
(25 mL) was added over a period of 0.5 h from a dropping funnel. After
the addition was completed, the reaction mixture was refluxed and stirred
overnight, filtered, and the solvent was evaporated to give a powder,
which was collected with hexane by filtration and washed several times
with water. The product was purified by crystallization from
hexane/ethylacetate to give 6-9 as pale yellow crystals. Compound (6).
Yellow crystals, yield 75%. 1H-NMR (CDCl3, ppm) δ: 8.86 (d, 4JHH = 2.5
Hz, 1H, ArH), 8.30 (dd, 3JHH = 9.0 Hz, 4JHH = 2.5 Hz, 1H, ArH), 8.03 (dd,
3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 3JHP = 14.5 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.68 (t, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 1H,
ArH), 7.45 (tt, 3JHH = 7.5 Hz, 4JHH = 2.5 Hz, 1H, ArH), 7.16 (t, 3JHH =
7.5 Hz, 1H, ArH), 6.92 (d, 3JHH = 9 Hz, 1H, ArH), 4.08 (m, 4H, POCH2CH3),
1.21 (t, 6H, POCH2CH3, 3JHH = 7.0 Hz). FAB-MS: m/z: 397.2 (100%, M + H+),
793.2 (2M + H+ 45%). m.p. 45-47°C.
