$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Diaryl ether formation proceeded cleanly upon treatment with CsF (6
equiv, DMSO, 25°C, 23 h, 75%) to provide a ≥6:1 mixture of P:M 18 with
the natural DE atropisomer. P-18: natural DE atropisomer configuration,
white film. P-18: [α]25 D +38 (c 0.05, CH3OH); 1H NMR (CD3OD, 293 K, 400
MHz) δ 8.10 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.88 (s, 1H), 7.61 (s, 1H), 7.54 (d, J =
7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.36 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H), 7.16-7.05 (m, 1H), 7.08 (dd, J =
8.6, 2.4 Hz, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1H), 6.95 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H),
6.90 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 6.62 (d, J = 2.2 Hz, 1H), 5.84 (s, 1H), 5.66
(s, 1H), 5.50-5.43 (m, 2H), 5.21 (s, 1H), 4.90-4.74 (m, 2H), 4.75 (s,
2H), 4.61 (br s, 2H), 4.33 (dd, J = 7.8, 4.0 Hz, 1H), 4.14 (s, 3H), 4.07
(s, 1H), 4.05 (dd, J = 10.2, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 3.92 (dd, J = 10.1, 4.0 Hz,
1H), 3.87 (s, 3H), 3.76-3.68 (m, 2H), 3.67 (s, 3H), 3.62 (s, 3H), 3.57
(t, J = 4.6 Hz, 2H), 3.36 (s, 3H), 2.88-2.78 (m, 1H), 2.78 (s, 3H), 2.64
(dd, J = 17.2, 8.0 Hz, 1H), 1.90-1.80 (m, 1H), 1.65-1.45 (m, 2H), 1.54
(s, 9H), 0.95 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 3H), 0.88 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H); IR (film) v
max 3296, 2924, 1651, 1533, 1503, 1482, 1323, 1234, 1158, 1082, 1058,
1021 cm-1; FABHRMS (NBA-CsI) m/z 1499.7314 (M+ + Cs, C66H16ClN9O21
requires 1499.7395). The 2D 1H-1H ROES Y NMR spectrum (CD3OD, 300 K, 600
MHz) displayed the following diagnostic nOe crosspeaks: C4a 5-H/C2 5-H (8
7.01/4.61, s), C4a 5-H/C2 6-H (8 7.01/4.07, s), C2 5-H/C2 6-H (8
4.61/4.07, s), C5a 6-H/C3 6-H (8 7.62/5.21, s), C5a 6-H/C2 6-H (8
7.62/4.07, m), C5a 2-H/C3 2-H (8 7.87/5.47, s).
