$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Preparation of
Substituted 2-(2-Halophenoxy)anilines 3. A suspension of substituted
1-fluoro(chloro)-2-nitrobenzene (20 mmol), substituted
2-iodo(bromo)phenol (20 mmol), and potassium carbonate (40 mmol) in
dimethylsulfoxide (30 mL) was heated at 100 °C for 8 h. After cooling to
room temperature, the reaction mixture was diluted with water (50 mL) and
extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 150 mL). The combined organic phase was
washed with water (3 × 100 mL) and dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate. The solvent was removed under reduced pressure to give crude
nitro halide used in the next step without further purification. The
solution of crude nitro halide and tin(ΙΙ) chloride dihydrate (100 mmol)
in ethyl acetate (100 mL) was stirred at room temperature for 18 h. The
reaction mixture was quenched with aqueous sodium hydroxide, and the
aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 100 mL). The combined
organic phase was washed with water (3 × 100 mL) and dried over anhydrous
magnesium sulfate. The solvent was evaporated in vacuo, and the residue
was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel with a mixture of
hexane and ethyl acetate as eluant to afford the corresponding product.
1-[3-Amino-4-(2-bromo-5-fluorophenoxy)phenyl]ethanone (3v). 75% yield; mp
82−83 °C; IR (neat) 1685 cm−1; 1H NMR (300MHz, CD3SOCD3) δ 7.77−7.71 (m,
1H), 7.45 (s, 1H), 7.16 (dd, J = 2.1, 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.03−6.97 (m, 1H),
6.78 (dd, J = 2.7, 9.3 Hz, 1H), 6.71 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 5.33 (s, 2H),
2.47 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (300MHz, CD3SOCD3) δ 197.85, 162.73 (d, J = 244.7
Hz), 154.54 (d, J = 10.5 Hz), 146.26, 140.46, 135.32 (d, J = 9.5 Hz),
134.66, 118.51, 118.22, 115.93, 113.21 (d, J = 22.3 Hz), 109.18 (d, J =
2.6 Hz), 107.99 (d, J = 25.9 Hz), 27.34; MS (EI) m/z 323 [M+], 325 [M+ +
2] ; HRMS Calcd. for C14H11BrFNO2 322.9957, found 322.9928.
