$DATUM 123-91-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the preparation of diaryl ether coupling products 2
A mixture of bromide 3 (100 mg, 0.39 mmol), p-allyl-phenol (4) (78 mg,
0.58 mmol), Cs2CO3 (253 mg, 0.78 mmol), CuI (7.4 mg, 0.039 mmol), and
N,N-dimethyl-glycine hydrochloride (16.3 mg, 0.12 mmol) in dioxane (2 mL)
in a sealed tube was heated at 90°C under nitrogen atmosphere for 48 h.
The cooled mixture was partitioned between EtOAc and water. The organic
layer was separated, and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc. The
combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and
concentrated in vacuo. Purification via flash column chromatography
(EtOAc : hexanes = 1 : 7) of the residue afforded Ullmann coupling
product 2a Colorless oil, 91 mg (75%). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.11 (d,
2H, J = 8.4 Hz), 6.90 (d, 2H, J = 8.4 Hz ), 6.54 (s, 1H), 6.41 (s, 1H),
5.86-6.00 (m, 2H), 4.98-5.12 (m, 4H), 3.87 (s, 3H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.37
(d, 2H, J = 6.5 Hz), 3.24 (d, 2H, J = 6.5 Hz); 13 C-NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz) δ
156.3, 153.8, 149.7, 139.4, 137.8, 137.1, 136.0, 134.4, 130.5, 117.7,
116.2, 115.8, 113.5, 108.3, 61.2, 56.3, 40.2, 39.6; MS (FAB+) m/z 310
(M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key step, product depends on solvent, Ullmann coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
