$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1. A mixture of 4-fluoro-2-methoxyphenol (54c) (1.34g, 9.4 mmol),
1,3-difluoro-5-nitrobenzene (55 e) (1.5 g, 9.4 mmol) in DMSO (5.0 mL) and
anhydrous K2CO3 (1.94 g, 1.4 mmol) was heated at 60 °C overnight. The
mixture was poured into ice water and extracted with EtOAc (3 × 50 mL).
The organic layer was sequentially washed with brine (2 × 75 mL), dried
over anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was
purified by column chromatography. 56f (2.0 g, 75%). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.58 (dt, J= 2.16, 8.14 Hz, 1H), 7.48 (td, J= 1.12, 2.16 Hz,
1H), 7.08 (dd, J= 5.65, 8.78 Hz, 1H), 6.91 (dt, J= 2.32, 9.39 Hz, 1H),
6.79 (dd, J= 2.84, 9.99 Hz, 1H), 6.72 (ddd, J= 2.85, 7.80, 8.75 Hz, 1H),
3.78 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.87, 162.04, 161.88, 160.28,
160.19, 160.09, 152.61, 152.53, 149.69, 149.60, 138.34, 138.31, 123.33,
123.25, 109.61, 109.41, 107.58, 107.40, 106.92, 106.89, 104.98, 104.76,
101.61, 101.39, 56.12.
