$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Bromo-4-chloro-1-(4-chloro-2-nitrophenoxy)-benzene (21). Water (1.2 mL)
was added to a mixture of 2-bromo-4-chlorophenol (13.81 g, 67.07 mmol)
and 1,4-dichloro-2-nitrobenzene (12.45 g, 65.20 mmol). Then, KOH (4.5 g)
was added in three portions with constant stirring. The mixture was
heated at 120 °C until the reaction was completed (TLC control,
CH2Cl2/hexane 1:1). Thereafter, the organic layer was extracted with NaOH
(2 mol/L, 3 × 50 mL), then dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated. The oily
product solidified on treatment with hexane (18.18 g, 75%).
2-Bromo-4-chloro-1-(4-chloro-2-nitrophenoxy)-benzene (21), yield (18.18
g, 75%). mp: 83-84 °C.
