$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Fc-diazo-OMe was synthesized by nucleophilic aromatic substitution (SNAr)
reaction of Fc-2Cl with Azo-OMe. The SNAr reaction was carried out with
potassium carbonate as the base in dimethylformamide at room temperature.
Termination of the SNAr reaction was monitored by observing the
disappearance of Fc-2Cl via thin-layer chromatography. The reaction
mixture was transferred into water after the end of reaction. The
resulting granular precipitate was filtered, and the solid product was
dried at room temperature. The crude product was finally purified by
column chromatography and further recrystallized using acetone/petroether
(1:5). Yield: 75 %; m.p. = 208-210 °C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): 8.00
(d, 4Hd), 7.91 (d, 4He), 7.50 (d, 4Hf), 7.15 (d, 4Hc), 6.46 (s, 4Hb),
5.31 (s, 5Ha), 3.89 (s, 6Hg), 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO-d6): 55.70 (2C12),
76.01 (5C1), 78.20 (4C2), 114.96 (4C10), 120.99 (4C5), 124.54 (4C6),
124.65 (4C9), 129.54 (2C3), 146.09 (2C8), 149.62 (2C7), 155.44 (2C4),
162.21 (2C11); FT-IR m(cm-1): 3,080.4 (C-H, aromatic), 2,959.2, 2,836.1
(C-H, -OCH3), 1,599.7, 1,532.8, 1,470.9 (-C = C-), 1,421.4 (-N=N-),
1,146.9 (O-C), 832.9 (P-F); ESI-MS (m/z): [M-PF6-]+ calculated for
[C37H31FeN4O4]+: 651.5109; found: 651.5095. Anal. Calc. for
C37H31F6FeN4O4P (796.4 g mol-1): C, 68.21; H, 4.80; N, 8.60, O, 9.82.
Found: C, 68.01; H, 4.57; N, 8.48; O, 9.71.
