$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Fc-diazo-OMe was synthesized by nucleophilic
aromatic substitution (SNAr) reaction of Fc-2Cl with Azo-OMe. The SNAr
reaction was carried out with potassium carbonate as the base in
dimethylformamide at room temperature. Termination of the SNAr reaction
was monitored by observing the disappearance of Fc-2Cl via thin-layer
chromatography. The reaction mixture was transferred into water after the
end of reaction. The resulting granular precipitate was filtered, and the
solid product was dried at room temperature. The crude product was
finally purified by column chromatography and further recrystallized
using acetone/petroether (1:5). Fc-diazo-H was synthesized by
nucleophilic aromatic substitution (SNAr) reaction of Fc-2Cl with Azo-H
in a manner similar to Fc-diazo-OMe. Yield: 5.42 g (75 %). mp = 203-205
°C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): 8.12 (d, 4He), 7.97 (d, 4Hd), 7.69-7.59
(m, 4Hf, 2Hg), 7.55 (d, 4Hc), 6.62 (s, 4Hb), 5.47 (s, 5Ha); 13C NMR (125
MHz, DMSO-d6): 76.23 (5C1), 78.27 (4C2), 120.94 (4C5), 122.58 (4C6),
124.94 (4C9), 129.40 (2C10), 129.52 (4C3), 131.72 (2C11), 149.45 (2C7),
151.86 (2C8), 156.13 (2C4); FT-IR m(cm-1): 3,087.8(C-H, aromatic),
1,585.7, 1,534.85, 1,470.5(-C = C-), 1,419.0(-N=N-), 1,150.8(O-C),
829.3(P-F); ESI-MS (m/z): [M-PF6-]+ calculated for [C35H27FeN4O2]+:
591.4589; found: 591.4570. Anal. Calc. for C35H27F6FeO2PN4 (736.4 g
mol-1): C, 71.07; H, 4.60; N, 9.47; O, 5.41. Found: C, 70.88; H, 4.47; N,
9.35; O, 5.31.
