$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (±)-Diisopropyl myricatomentogenin (23). To a solution of S6 (120 mg,
0.28 mmol) in pyridine (40 mL, 0.007 M) was added K2CO3 (99 mg, 0.71
mmol). The mixture was was heated to 90 °C for 10 min, CuO (56 mg 0.71
mmol) was added and mixture was heated to reflux. After 69 h TLC
indicated consumption of starting material. The reaction mixture was
cooled to rt and quenched with 2M HCl solution (3 ml). T7he mixture was
diluted with H2O and extracted with EtOAc (50 mL x 3). The organic layers
were combined, washed with H2O, saturated NaCl solution, dried over
MgSO4, filtered and concentrated. Purification by FCC (6:1 Hexanes:EtOAc)
yielded (±)-23. white solid, yield 89 mg, 0.21 mmol, 74%. Rf 0.66 (2:1
Hexanes: EtOAc); mp = 91-94 °C IR (thin film) 2974, 1717, 1580; 1H NMR
(700 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.96 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 6.86 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1 H),
6.78 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1 H), 6.65 (dd, J = 2.2, 8.1 Hz, 1 H), 5.64 (d, J =
2.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.65 (sept, J = 6.1 Hz, 1 H), 4.43 (sept, J = 6.2 Hz, 1 H),
3.73 (s, 3 H), 3.16 (td, J = 5.5, 12.9 Hz, 1 H), 3.07 (dd, J = 9.9, 16.0
Hz, 1 H), 2.70 (ddd, J = 1.5, 8.6, 16.1 Hz, 1 H), 2.40-2.30 (m, 3 H),
2.15 (ddd, J = 6.0, 10.8, 19.2 Hz, 1 H), 1.80-1.75 (m, 1 H), 1.71-1.66
(m, 2 H), 1.56-1.50 (m, 2 H), 1.42 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 9 H), 1.23 (J = 6.1
Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR (176 MHz, CDCl3) δ 210.4, 151.6, 150.5, 147.8, 146.6,
144.6, 134.9, 133.2, 125.5, 121.5, 119.6, 117.6, 113.6, 75.3, 72.3, 60.2,
46.3, 41.0, 31.2, 27.2, 25.1, 23.2, 22.3, 22.3, 22.2, 19.2; HRMS (ESI)
calcd for C26H34O5 [M+H]: 427.2486, found 427.2484.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Chirality in Diarylether Heptanoids: Synthesis of Myricatomentogenin,
Jugcathanin, and Congeners
