$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Synthesis of Diaryl
Ethers: An oven-dried test tube, which was equipped with a magnetic stir
bar and fitted with a teflon screw-cap, was charged with L8 (1.5-7.5 mol
%), [(cinnamyl)PdCl]2 (0.5-2.5 mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg, 1.5 mmol), aryl
halide (1.0 mmol) and phenol (1.5 mmol). The vessel was evacuated and
backfilled with argon (this process was repeated a total of three times)
after which toluene and DME were added via syringe (the amount of solvent
is specific to each substrate). The solution was stirred at the specified
temperature for 16 h after which it was cooled to rt and diluted with
ethyl acetate, washed with water, filtered through a pad of silica gel
(eluted with diethyl ether), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
crude material was purified by flash chromatography via the Biotage SP4.
1-isopropyl-2-(2-(trifluoromethyl)phenoxy)benzene (9).11 Following the
General Procedure, a mixture of 2-bromobenzotrifluoride (140 μL g, 1.0
mmol), 2-i-Pr-phenol (200 μL, 1.5 mmol), L8 (3.0 mol %), [(C6H9)PdCl]2
(1.0 mol %), K3PO4 (318 mg), toluene (0.6 mL) and DME (0.3 mL) was
stirred at room temperature for 24 h. The crude product was purified via
the Biotage SP4 (silica-packed 25 g snap column; 0-5% EtOAc/hexanes) to
provide the title compound as a colorless oil (208 mg, 74%). 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3) δ: 7.69 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.46 - 7.37 (m, 2H), 7.25 - 7.17
(m, 2H), 7.12 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 6.92 - 6.90 (m, 1H), 6.78 (d, J = 8.4
Hz, 1H), 3.25 (dt, J = 13.8, 6.9 Hz, 1H), 1.25 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 6H) ppm.
13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 156.5, 152.8, 140.8, 133.4, 127.6, 127.5 (q,
J = 5 Hz), 127.3, 125.3, 123.8 (q, J = 272 Hz), 120.4 (q, J = 31 Hz),
121.9, 120.3, 117.1, 27.5, 23.0 ppm. 19F NMR (CDCl3, 282 MHz): δ -62.36
(s) ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 3074, 2966, 2872, 2361, 2337, 2048, 1919, 1806,
1698, 1684, 1609, 1580, 1485, 1458, 1385, 1364, 1322, 1269, 1246, 1135,
1084, 1055, 1036, 947 cm-1. Anal. Calcd. for C16H15F3O: C, 68.56; H,
5.39. Found: C, 68.49; H, 5.48.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A New Biarylphosphine Ligand for the Pd-Catalyzed Synthesis of Diaryl
Ethers under Mild Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Salvi, Luca; Davis, Nicole R.; Ali, Siraj Z.; Buchwald, Stephen L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(1), 170-173

