$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Experimental Procedure for the O-Arylation of
Aryl Bromides with Various Phenols (Table 2). To an oven-dried screwed
vial were added bromoarenes (0.2 mmol), phenol (0.3 mmol), sodium
tert-butoxide (38 mg, 0.4 mmol), Rh2(OAc)4 (3.2 mg, 3 mol %),
N,N-dicyclohexylbenzimidazolium hexafluorophosphate (8 mg, 10 mol %),
AgPF6 (5 mg, 10 mol %) and toluene (0.2 mL). The mixture was vigorously
stirred at 100 °C for 24 h and diluted with ethyl acetate. The crude
reaction mixture was filtered through a pad of silica gel, and then
organic solvents were removed in vacuo followed by silica gel column
chromatography (ethyl acetate/n-hexane). 1-Methoxy-4-phenoxybenzene (3a,
Table 2).1 The title compound was purified by silica gel column
chromatography (EtOAc/n-Hx, 1:10).
1-(4-Methoxyphenoxy)-3,5-bis(trifluoromethyl)benzene (3d, Table 2). The
title compound was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(EtOAc/n-Hx, 1:10). colorless oil (49 mg, 74%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.55 (1H, s), 7.35 (2H, m), 7.06-7.03 (2H, m), 7.00-6.97 (2H, m), 3.87
(3H, s); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.7, 157.0, 147.9, 133.5 (q, 2 J
C-F = 33.4 Hz), 127.0 (q, 1 J C-F = 271.0 Hz), 121.4, 116.9, 115.6 (q, 3
J C-F = 3.6 Hz), 115.5, 55.6; IR (Film) ν 2840, 1616, 1506, 1374, 1278,
1187, 1133, 951, 838, 681 cm-1; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for C15H10F6O2
[M]+: 336.0587, found: 336.0585.
