$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure to prepare G1 or G2
dendrimers. One equivalent of the core molecule, two equivalents of
3,5-bis(t-butyl)phenol or the dendron (G1 or G2) and 3 equivalents of
K2CO3 were refluxed in a mixture of DMF:toluene (2:1) under Dean-Stark
conditions. After refluxing for 5-48h (TLC control), the reaction mixture
was evaporated in vacuum. CH2Cl2 was added and extracted with H2O. The
organic layer was separated, dried over MgSO4 and evaporated in vacuum.
After purification by column chromatography dendrimers of the different
generation were obtained. G1-dendrimer (17c). Yield: 74%. 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.69 (t, 2H), 8.22 (d, 4H), 8.07 (t, 4H), 7.99 (d, 8H),
7.65 (t, 4H), 7.29 (d, 4H), 1.41 (s, 72H); MS (ESI) m/z 1432.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key step, Dean-Stark trap used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dendrimers Containing 1,3,4-Oxadiazoles
